<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- PMDA batch P2 violations fixture: one dedicated violator per rule, exactly one
     finding each when evaluated as 2.1 (the four 2.1-only rules DD0122/DD0125/
     DD0131/DD0139 are version-gated off when the same document is evaluated as 2.0).
     Construct map:
       OD0022  second Study with duplicate OID ST.P2V
       OD0027  second MetaDataVersion with duplicate OID MDV.1
       OD0030  IG.DUPOID x2 (distinct SASDatasetNames XA/XB)
       OD0031  IT.DUPOID x2 (referenced once from IG.HOST)
       OD0032  CL.DUPOID x2 (distinct Names)
       DD0131  CL.NAME1/CL.NAME2 sharing Name "Duplicate Name List"
       OD0079  CL.TERMDUP with EnumeratedItem M,M
       OD0079-B CL.TERMDUP2 with CodeListItem A,A
       DD0012  MDV-level def:leaf LF.DUP x2 (referenced from COM.DOC's DocumentRef)
       DD0013  MT.DUP x2 (referenced from IG.KEY ItemRef)
       DD0083  COM.DUP x2 (referenced from IG.SAS1)
       DD0014  VL.DUP x2 (referenced from IT.VLDREF)
       DD0051  IG.SAS1/IG.SAS2 sharing SASDatasetName SAME
       DD0062  IG.SAS1 Description with two xml:lang="en" TranslatedText
       DD0041  IG.KEY ItemRefs with KeySequence 1,1
       OD0041  IG.ITEMDUP ItemRefs both IT.COMMON
       OD0042  IG.ORD ItemRefs with OrderNumber 1,1
       DD0088  RD.DUP x2   DD0089  RD.N1/RD.N2 sharing Name "Table 9"
       DD0091  RD.HOST with AR.DUP x2
       DD0095  AnalysisDataset -> IG.MISSING     DD0097  AnalysisVariable -> IT.MISSING
       DD0015  MT.DOC DocumentRef -> LF.MISSING  DD0016  ItemRef MethodOID -> MT.MISSING
       DD0017  IT.VLREF ValueListRef -> VL.MISSING
       DD0018  IG.ARCH def:ArchiveLocationID -> LF.NOWHERE
       DD0071  IT.CMT def:CommentOID -> COM.MISSING
       DD0122  IG.STD def:StandardOID -> STD.MISSING
       DD0125  CL.WRONGSTD def:StandardOID -> STD.SDTM (Type IG, not CT)
       OD0046  IG.SAS2 ItemRef -> IT.NOWHERE     OD0048  IT.CLREF CodeListRef -> CL.MISSING
       orphans DD0067 IT.ORPHAN / DD0078 LF.ORPHAN / DD0079 COM.ORPHAN /
               DD0080 MT.ORPHAN / DD0081 VL.ORPHAN / DD0082 CL.ORPHAN /
               DD0139 STD.ORPHAN
     Everything else is referenced/unique so no rule fires twice: STD.CT is kept
     referenced via CL.TERMDUP's def:StandardOID (Type CT, DD0125-negative). -->
